      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "District 2 is most likely to become a primary hotspot due to its very high density, large population of essential workers unable to work from home, and barriers like limited English proficiency that hinder public health messaging. Even though District 1 has certain advantages like high insurance, the intense physical contact and lack of mitigation measures in District 2 create higher transmission risk. District 3 could experience secondary spread as a delivery point of infection from these high-risk areas, though its lower density offers some buffer. Therefore, the simulation should prioritize monitoring and intervention resources in District 2 first.",
